   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Cooperative Work Agency (CWA) has developed an Amended draft of the Decree Law No (20) of 2017 on Cooperatives, and prepared draft by-laws for the establishment of the Cooperative Development Fund and the Cooperative Training Institute. 
The National Cooperative Sectoral Strategy has been revised and updated to cover the years 2021-2023 in accordance with the Prime Minister&apos;s Office instructions, and in line with the national priorities
Participatory Rapid Assessment has been conducted of the Impacts of the COVID-19 Pandemic on the Cooperative Sector.
Capacity of CWA and GCU members to support primary cooperatives in developing and designing internal plan in line with the updated sectoral strategy has been strengthened through a 4-day strategic planning training The ILO has supported the CWA in revising the sectoral strategy for the years 2021-2023, and through the revision of the legal framework governing the sector. The ILO has hired a local legal consultant, an international expert on the Cooperative Law, and the national consultant on cooperatives to lead and facilitate the revision process. The ILO supported the revision of the Cooperative Law and the formulation of the pertinent secondary legislation, including the by-laws of the two promotional entities of the Agency, the Cooperative Development Fund (CDF) and the Cooperative Training Institute (CTI).
In light of the COVID-19 pandemic, and the damage it has done to the cooperative sector, the ILO has conducted the rapid assessment study in support to the CWA to study the impacts of the pandemic on the cooperative sector, and draw recommendations based on the findings for recovery and mitigating the impacts of the pandemic. 
To support the successful implementation of the national sectoral strategy, the ILO has designed a training for the CWA and GCU members to be able to support cooperatives in designing their internal strategic plans.</narrative>
